# upstream/90-operation-equivalence-iterative: OperationEquivalence
# compares operations and regions from an explicit stack, so its native
# depth does not grow with the IR's nesting, and the e-graph's comparison
# of a match's case bodies and the deduplication of functions keep a small
# stack. Over chains nested 10,000 deep, on a thread whose stack is
# 256 KiB, two chains alike are equivalent by both entry points, with
# every value marked once in the order the recursion marked them, and a
# chain that differs only in its innermost branch is not
# (equivalence.cpp). The chains are built in memory: mlir-opt's parser
# recurses on the same depth through each operation's parse hook, so
# through mlir-opt the comparison is never seen alone.
# Building a program against MLIR's libraries takes longer than a step.
step_limit=180
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
mlir_check "operation equivalence: chains nested 10,000 deep on a 256 KiB stack, alike by both entry points with each value marked once in order, and one differing innermost not" \
  "$here/equivalence.cpp" 10000
